Z||000000||fiero56||09-23-2001||07:45 PM||||My formula is almost completed, and then I will have nothing to occupy my free time. Working on them is almost/sometimes is more fun than driving them. I picked up an '86SE v-6 4-speed last year with no plans for it until recently. I've kicked around a few ideas, but haven't committed to anything yet.<P>The most likely course will be convert it to fastback(doh!), paint it a different color(yellow is promising right now), rebuild the bottom end with neutrally balanced crank, convert to auto(looks like a 4T60 is probable), rebuild suspension, and get rid of the 14" wheels. <P>If I don't find a family member who wants it, there will probably be a Fiero for sale. <P>Any other ideas I should kick around for this beast? I don't plan to sink a ton of money in it, at this point I don't plan to keep it once its finished.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SEmon_2.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-23-2001||08:22 PM||||Stereo.  10" sub in the firewall, amp on the other side, 5 1/4" components in AusFieros' door pods, etc.  The sub box and amp rack will take up some of your time and you'll get more out of the car when you try to sell it.||||reg||1
